WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.000
ASDRP / NEUROSCIENCE PORTFOLIO
Study the brain. Build for people.
A connected research and communication portfolio with reproducible evidence.

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:08.000
FLAGSHIP
Behavior improves prediction across three mice.
Held-out correlation rises 0.126 → 0.158, 0.154 → 0.203, and 0.143 → 0.191.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:12.000
COMPLEMENTARY STUDY
EEG results stay honest.
The pointwise model reaches 0.625 final-block ROC AUC; causal context reaches 0.530.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.000
DEEPER ANALYSIS
Controls and timescales matter.
Behavior shuffles erase the mouse gain; EEG blocked folds and window sweeps expose variability.

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.000
TRANSLATION
Research should be inspectable and usable.
Neurocomms and Neurodivergent patterns inform accessible mobile, HTML, presentation, and video artifacts.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:24.000
REPRODUCIBILITY
Every claim has a trail.
Reports, code, manifests, metrics, figures, captions, an Android build, and a release audit are public.

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:28.000
NEXT
Keep testing without overstating.
Add animals, recordings, hierarchical uncertainty, applicant narration, and personal application details.

